EMPIRE 64
Type:     Commodore 64 trading / strategy simulation
Origin:   Type-in program, Ahoy magazine, October 1987 (originally C128)
Author:   Cleveland M. Blakemore
Port:     Richard J. Derocher / Binary Legends (C64, 2026)
Share:    https://rickyderocher.itch.io/empire-64

GOAL
Acquire 100% of Empire land shares within one in-game year
(four seasons: spring, summer, fall, winter).

CORE VARIABLES
starting_cash     $500 to $10,000 (player choice)
guild_credit      $5000 (debt notes; cannot buy land with them)
land_shares       deeds measured in furlongs; win at 100%
inventory         goods + cash
season            changes map border color and prices
  spring          green
  summer          yellow
  fall            brown
  winter          white

COMMODITIES (9)
Artifacts
Weapons           swords, spears
Armor
Rare Metals       gold, silver
Horses
Tools
Food Products     grain, rice, etc.
Fabrics           clothing, drapes
Land Shares

FUNDAMENTALS
- Player is a traveling merchant on a joystick-controlled world map (Port 2).
- Terrain changes sprite (horse on land, canoe on water).
- Enter a kingdom through a doorway; clock pauses inside.
- Menu: Buy, Sell, Seasonal Changes, Inquire, Inventory, Bid Farewell.
- Each kingdom produces one unique good; Inquire shows demand and base price.
- Bargain with joystick: up/down = tens, left/right = ones, fire = confirm.
- Buy low, sell high; winter raises food and fabric demand.
- Must visit another kingdom before re-entering the same one.
- Game ends after winter; report shows cash, inventory, and Empire %.
- Typical session: 20–30 minutes real time.

